  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_338e4eef917d4614a66ce8ba8cd9496d",
      "statement": "In Kafka only the producer is transactional; exactly-once comes from the producer transactionally updating the consumer's committed offset, with one producer per consumer recommended.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/design/design.md#L209-L223",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3c40487f537301ef7ab2a62a60caaf428205f911b6a8eca727b793ac78cd023c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ea90d5f05c694ed7b9caccd043f5d17d",
      "statement": "Exactly-once consumers must set isolation.level=read_committed and enable.auto.commit=false, and the producer's transactional.id makes a restarted application abort in-flight transactions of the previous instance.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/design/design.md#L225-L227",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c7ffdb07739d81edb4da3dba05895c8b588bae6d850c9aab06c5fed4652775da:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9b51da647d9542d49df22944f5decf65",
      "statement": "After an aborted transaction the application must explicitly reset the consumer position, either by recreating clients or by seeking to committed offsets.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/design/design.md#L231-L231",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:67e4f951e3bd9ec6a6e75789b9f44923c2c003321b19a96413a33f64798a0de4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/design/design.md#L245-L245",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:01ba4719c80b6fe911b091a7c05124b64eeece964e09c058ef8f9805daca546b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0743f811954245a8acfac93565b2d03f",
      "statement": "Transactional exceptions are categorized as RetriableException and RefreshRetriableException (handled internally), AbortableException (abort and reset), ApplicationRecoverableException (restart producer), InvalidConfigurationException and KafkaException.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/design/design.md#L233-L241",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3a0b97d058e976933617a3dc1f69e0339b2e4171e29374809c3c2d8f85a2b9aa:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_af13c3e2f9c44ec6ba216ad63d7decdc",
      "statement": "ExactlyOnceMessageProcessor calls initTransactions once, then per batch beginTransaction, send, sendOffsetsToTransaction with consumer.groupMetadata() and commitTransaction, aborting and rewinding on KafkaException.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://examples/src/main/java/kafka/examples/ExactlyOnceMessageProcessor.java#L113-L170",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:16291e410b9e285569a5278c3f9ab80c4c4a1ce6132fa9269cdf4c9365b661e9:"
